* Project queues for quarqueueus. Mounted into /etc/mqm/ and re-applied on every start.
* DEFINE ... REPLACE resets every attribute not listed here to its default,
* so this file is the single source of truth: don't change these queues in the console.

* Job requests from the REST API to the worker route.
* After 3 failed (rolled-back) deliveries the JMS client moves the message to the backout queue.
DEFINE QLOCAL('DEV.JOBS.REQUEST') +
       DEFPSIST(YES) +
       BOTHRESH(3) BOQNAME('DEV.JOBS.BACKOUT') +
       REPLACE

* Poison messages from DEV.JOBS.REQUEST. Inspect, fix, and move back by hand.
DEFINE QLOCAL('DEV.JOBS.BACKOUT') +
       DEFPSIST(YES) +
       REPLACE

* The JMS client requeues poison messages with their original context, which needs PASSALL
* on the target. The image's DEV.** profile only grants BROWSE,GET,INQ,PUT, and the most
* specific matching profile wins, so these records repeat those and add PASSALL.
* Without them the requeue fails (AMQ8077W ... passall, JMSWMQ1079/1080) and the listener loops.
* DEV.DEAD.LETTER.QUEUE is the client's fallback when the backout queue can't be used.
SET AUTHREC PROFILE('DEV.JOBS.BACKOUT') OBJTYPE(QUEUE) PRINCIPAL('app') +
    AUTHADD(BROWSE,GET,INQ,PUT,PASSALL)
SET AUTHREC PROFILE('DEV.DEAD.LETTER.QUEUE') OBJTYPE(QUEUE) PRINCIPAL('app') +
    AUTHADD(BROWSE,GET,INQ,PUT,PASSALL)
